+# Tool Input Validation
+
+| Field  | Value                |
+| ------ | -------------------- |
+| Issue  | re-cinq/HALEngine#37 |
+| Status | In Progress          |
+
+`ToolRegistry.execute` validates incoming tool input against the declared `inputSchema` before invoking the executor. A call whose input does not satisfy the schema is returned to the model as a `ToolResponse` describing the constraint that failed; the executor is never invoked, and no input value ever appears in the returned text.
+
+## Validation Contract
+
+- When `execute` is called with input that is missing a required field, it returns a `ToolResponse` whose `result` names the missing field and the executor is never called ([validated by: returns a ToolResponse naming the missing required field and never calls the executor](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L4)).
+
+- The text returned on a validation failure never contains the offending input value, so a field holding user-identifying data cannot leak from the registry into the conversation ([validated by: never includes the offending value in the returned ToolResponse](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L27)).
+
+- When an orchestrated conversation contains a tool call that the registry rejects, `processMessage` resolves rather than throws, and the rejection text is part of the tool result the provider receives on the next round so the model can self-correct ([validated by: resolves processMessage when a corrected call follows a rejected one, with rejection text visible to the provider](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.acceptance.test.ts#L9)).
